  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Name three important zoonotic diseases prevalent in Bhutan. How would you prevent rabies in your community? (3 marks)', 'Important zoonotic diseases in Bhutan: rabies (especially in the southern border districts), scrub typhus, brucellosis, anthrax, taeniasis/cysticercosis and avian influenza.
Prevention of rabies in the community:
• Mass vaccination of dogs (and cats), registration and responsible pet ownership.
• Control of the stray-dog population through sterilisation and the national dog population management programme; proper waste disposal so dogs are not attracted.
• Public awareness: avoid stray dogs, report suspected rabid animals and all bites.
• After any bite or scratch: wash the wound immediately with soap and running water for 15 minutes, apply an antiseptic, and go to the nearest health centre for post-exposure prophylaxis (anti-rabies vaccine, plus rabies immunoglobulin for severe bites) - completing the full course.
• Pre-exposure vaccination of high-risk groups such as veterinary staff and dog catchers; coordination between health and livestock sectors (One Health).', null, '[{"point": "Zoonoses in Bhutan (any three): rabies, scrub typhus, brucellosis, anthrax, cysticercosis/taeniasis, avian influenza, leptospirosis", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Rabies prevention (animal side): mass dog vaccination, dog population control/sterilisation (e.g. nationwide accelerated dog population management), responsible pet ownership, control of stray dogs", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Rabies prevention (human side): immediate washing of bite wounds with soap and water for 15 min, timely post-exposure prophylaxis (anti-rabies vaccine ± immunoglobulin), awareness, reporting bites, pre-exposure vaccine for high-risk workers", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
