  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Differentiate between:

a) CT scan and PET scan (1 marks)', 'a) CT (computed tomography) scan uses X-rays taken from many angles and a computer to produce cross-sectional images showing the structure (anatomy) of organs. PET (positron emission tomography) uses an injected radioactive tracer such as fluorodeoxyglucose; it shows the function or metabolic activity of tissues, e.g. spread of cancer or brain activity.', null, '[{"point": "CT uses X-rays to give detailed cross-sectional anatomical images; PET uses an injected radioactive tracer (e.g. FDG) to show metabolic/functional activity (cancer, brain)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
