  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Differentiate between:

c) Implants and prostheses (1 marks)', 'c) Implants are medical devices placed inside the body, partly or wholly, to replace or support a structure or function - e.g. pacemaker, intraocular lens, hip joint, dental implant. Prostheses are artificial substitutes for a missing body part, often external and removable - e.g. artificial leg or arm, artificial eye, denture.', null, '[{"point": "Implants are devices placed inside the body (pacemaker, artificial joint, dental implant, lens); prostheses replace a missing body part, often external (artificial limb, eye)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
