  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Write short notes on telemedicine and video-conferencing and their application in patient care in the Bhutanese context. (3 marks)', 'Telemedicine is the use of information and communication technology (internet, phone, digital imaging) to provide healthcare at a distance - remote consultation, diagnosis (e.g. sending X-rays, ECGs or photographs to a specialist), treatment advice, referral and follow-up.
Video-conferencing is a real-time audio and video link that lets doctors, specialists, health workers and patients at different places see and talk to each other; it is also used for training, case discussions and meetings.
Application in Bhutan: Bhutan''s mountainous terrain, scattered villages and shortage of specialists make travel to referral hospitals difficult and costly. Telemedicine and video-conferencing link Basic Health Units and district hospitals with JDWNRH and the regional referral hospitals so that health assistants can get specialist advice, emergencies can be managed and referred faster, unnecessary travel is avoided, and staff in remote areas receive continuing medical education. Challenges include internet connectivity, equipment, power supply and training of staff.', null, '[{"point": "Telemedicine: delivery of healthcare at a distance using ICT - remote consultation, diagnosis (tele-radiology, tele-ECG), referral and follow-up", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Video-conferencing: real-time audio-video link allowing doctors/specialists to see and talk to patients and health workers in remote places, plus training and case discussions", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Bhutanese context: mountainous terrain and few specialists - links BHUs/district hospitals with JDWNRH and regional referral hospitals, reduces travel and cost, speeds emergency advice and referral, continuing medical education; challenges - connectivity, equipment, training", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
